[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Manic Microbes
GenericName=Artificial Life Simulator
Comment=A closed jar with one tap on it: light in, heat out, matter conserved
Exec=mm-app
Icon=com.manicmicrobes.ManicMicrobes
# One main category, or the entry can appear twice in the menu — Science is the main one and
# Biology is a subcategory of it. The AppStream file lists Education as well, which is a
# different job: that decides which shelf a software centre puts it on, not the menu.
Categories=Science;Biology;
Keywords=artificial life;alife;evolution;simulation;emergence;genome;
Terminal=false
# StartupWMClass ties a running window back to this entry so the taskbar shows this icon rather
# than a generic one. It has to equal what the window reports as its WM_CLASS, and a wrong value
# matches nothing — which is worse than leaving it out, because without it the desktop falls back
# to its own heuristics. Left out until it has been read off a running window with `xprop`.
